                    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <span class="last-updated">Last updated: October 25, 2026</span>

                    <p>At Kidamame, your privacy and the privacy of your children are extremely important to us. This
                        Privacy Policy explains, in plain language, what information is (and is not) handled when you
                        use the <strong>Kidamame Discovery</strong> app and our website <strong>kidamame.com</strong>.
                        It is designed to comply with the U.S. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act
                        (<strong>COPPA</strong>), the EU General Data Protection Regulation (<strong>GDPR</strong>),
                        the UK GDPR, the California Consumer Privacy Act (<strong>CCPA/CPRA</strong>), and the
                        Apple App Store Kids Category and Google Play Families policies.</p>

                    <div class="legal-highlight">
                        <div class="legal-highlight-icon">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="legal-highlight-content">
                            <p><strong>Our Promise to Parents:</strong> We <strong>do not collect, store, share, or
                                    sell any personal data</strong> from children or adults through our app. No
                                accounts, no advertising, no analytics, no app event tracking, no profiling.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- AT A GLANCE -->
                    <h2 id="at-a-glance">Privacy at a Glance</h2>
                    <ul class="legal-glance" role="list">
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-user-slash"></i><span><strong>No personal data</strong>We do not
                                collect names, emails, photos, location or device identifiers.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-eye-slash"></i><span><strong>No tracking</strong>No analytics, no
                                app event tracking, no advertising IDs, no attribution SDKs.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-ban"></i><span><strong>No ads</strong>The app contains no
                                advertising of any kind.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-user-lock"></i><span><strong>No accounts</strong>No sign-up,
                                no login, no user profiles.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-credit-card"></i><span><strong>Store payments</strong>Purchases
                                are processed entirely by Apple and Google.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-mobile-screen"></i><span><strong>Stays on device</strong>Progress
                                and unlock status are saved only locally.</span></li>
                    </ul>

                    <!-- 1 -->
                    <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who We Are</h2>
                    <p>Kidamame&reg; is a trademark of <strong>Marco Uberti</strong>, who is responsible for this
                        Privacy Policy.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>VAT number:</strong> 04896640168 &middot; <strong>REA:</strong> BG 498984</li>
                        <li><strong>Privacy contact:</strong> <a
                                href="mailto:support@kidamame.com">support@kidamame.com</a></li>
                    </ul>

                    <!-- 2 -->
                    <h2 id="no-data">2. Information We Do Not Collect</h2>
                    <p>Kidamame Discovery is built from the ground up as a safe, calm, and private space. We
                        <strong>do not collect, receive, or store any personal information</strong>, including:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Names, email addresses, phone numbers, postal addresses, or dates of birth;</li>
                        <li>Photos, videos, audio recordings, contacts, or precise or approximate location;</li>
                        <li>Advertising identifiers (Apple IDFA, Google Advertising ID) or any persistent identifier
                            used to recognize a user over time or across apps;</li>
                        <li>Behavioral data, usage analytics, or user profiles.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>No app event tracking.</strong> We do not track or log in-app events of any kind: no
                        screen views, taps, session lengths, gameplay progress, purchase events, or custom events are
                        sent to us or to any third party. The app contains <strong>no analytics SDKs</strong>,
                        <strong>no advertising or attribution SDKs</strong>, and
                        <strong>no social features or chat</strong>.</p>
                    <p><strong>No Unity Diagnostics.</strong> We do not use Unity Cloud Diagnostics, Unity crash
                        reporting, or any other third-party crash-reporting or performance-monitoring service.</p>

                    <!-- 3 -->
                    <h2 id="local-storage">3. Data Stored Only on Your Device</h2>
                    <p>To work properly, the app saves a small amount of non-personal application state exclusively
                        on your device, such as:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Whether premium content has been unlocked (true/false);</li>
                        <li>Local exploration progress within scenes and basic app settings.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>This information contains no personal or device identifiers, is never transmitted to us, and is
                        deleted when you uninstall the app.</p>

                    <!-- 4 -->
                    <h2 id="iap">4. In-App Purchases (Unity IAP)</h2>
                    <p>Kidamame Discovery offers an optional, one-time in-app purchase to unlock full access. To
                        connect the app to the native store billing systems we use the <strong>Unity In-App
                            Purchasing SDK, version 5.3.1</strong>.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Unity IAP acts only as a bridge between the app and <strong>Apple StoreKit</strong> or
                            <strong>Google Play Billing</strong>, to show the product price, start the purchase, and
                            restore previous purchases.</li>
                        <li>In our configuration, Unity IAP is <strong>not used to collect personal data, analytics,
                                or tracking information</strong>, and it is not connected to Unity Analytics or any
                            other Unity Gaming Services data product.</li>
                        <li>We do not receive any information that identifies who made a purchase.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Learn more:
                        <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.purchasing@5.3/manual/index.html"
                            target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unity IAP 5.3 documentation</a>,
                        <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.purchasing@5.3/changelog/CHANGELOG.html"
                            target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unity IAP changelog</a>, and
                        <a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">Unity Game Player and App User Privacy Policy</a>.
                    </p>

                    <!-- 5 -->
                    <h2 id="payments">5. Payment Processing by Apple &amp; Google</h2>
                    <p>All payments are processed <strong>directly and exclusively by Apple</strong> (App Store) or
                        <strong>Google</strong> (Google Play), using the account already set up on the device.
                        <strong>We never see, collect, process, or store</strong> credit card numbers, payment
                        details, billing addresses, or your Apple ID / Google account information.</p>
                    <p>Purchases are protected by the store's own authentication (password, Face ID, Touch ID, or
                        fingerprint). Parents can further control purchases with
                        <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/105055" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple Ask to
                            Buy &amp; Screen Time</a> or
                        <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/1075738" target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">Google Play parental controls</a>.
                        From the stores we only receive aggregated, non-identifying sales reports (e.g., number of
                        purchases per country).</p>
                    <p>Payment data is governed by the
                        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple Privacy
                            Policy</a> and the
                        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy
                            Policy</a>.
                    </p>

                    <!-- 6 -->
                    <h2 id="technical">6. Unity Engine &amp; Technical Network Requests</h2>
                    <p>The app is built with the <strong>Unity Engine</strong> and is configured in
                        <strong>Child-Directed / COPPA-compliant mode</strong>. Although we do not collect any data
                        ourselves, the Unity runtime and Unity IAP may occasionally make <strong>technical network
                            calls</strong>, for example:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Initialization or connectivity "pings" and configuration checks needed for the engine and
                            the purchasing module to start correctly;</li>
                        <li>Requests needed to complete, validate, or restore an in-app purchase.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>These requests may technically involve transient information such as an IP address and basic
                        device details (e.g., OS version, device model). This information is processed by Unity solely
                        for <strong>support for the internal operations</strong> of the app &mdash; maintaining
                        technical functionality, security, and integrity &mdash; which is expressly permitted without
                        parental consent under the COPPA exception in
                        <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-16/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-312"
                            target="_blank" rel="noopener">16 CFR &sect; 312.2 and &sect; 312.5(c)(7)</a>.
                        It is <strong>never</strong> used for behavioral advertising, profiling, or cross-app
                        tracking, and it is not shared with us.</p>
                    <p>Unity's processing is governed by the
                        <a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">Unity Game Player and App User Privacy Policy</a> and
                        <a href="https://unity.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unity Privacy
                            Policy</a>.
                    </p>

                    <!-- 7 -->
                    <h2 id="os-diagnostics">7. Operating System Crash Reports</h2>
                    <p>Like every app on iOS and Android, the device operating system may generate basic crash reports
                        if you have enabled diagnostic sharing in your device settings. These reports are managed by
                        Apple and Google under their own policies, contain technical data only (e.g., device model, OS
                        version, crash stack trace), and may be shared with us only in aggregated or anonymized form,
                        which we use solely to fix bugs. You can turn this off at any time in your device's privacy or
                        diagnostics settings.</p>

                    <!-- 8 -->
                    <h2 id="children">8. Children's Privacy (COPPA)</h2>
                    <p>Kidamame Discovery is made for children, and it is designed so that <strong>no personal
                            information is ever collected from them</strong>. There are no ads, no accounts, no chat, and
                        nothing a child can share. This is how the app meets COPPA, GDPR, the Apple App Store Kids
                        Category guidelines, and the Google Play Families Policy.</p>
                    <p>Parents and guardians are always welcome to write to us at
                        <a href="mailto:support@kidamame.com">support@kidamame.com</a>.</p>

                    <!-- 9 -->
                    <h2 id="your-rights">9. Your Privacy Rights (GDPR, UK GDPR &amp; CCPA)</h2>
                    <p>Since the app does not collect personal data, there is simply nothing about you for us to
                        access, correct, or delete. We <strong>never sell or share</strong> personal information and
                        never use it for advertising.</p>
                    <p>If you email us, you can ask at any time to see or delete your message. You also have the right
                        to contact your local data protection authority (in Italy, the
                        <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Garante per la
                            protezione dei dati personali</a>).</p>

                    <!-- 10 -->
                    <h2 id="website">10. Our Website</h2>
                    <p>When you visit <strong>kidamame.com</strong>:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> we use a consent tool (Cookiebot) and only strictly necessary
                            cookies. We do not use analytics, advertising, or profiling cookies. See our
                            <a href="/cookie/">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> we do not collect emails on our site. Subscribing redirects you
                            to Substack, which handles your data under its own
                            <a href="https://substack.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
                            You can unsubscribe at any time from any email.</li>
                        <li><strong>Support emails:</strong> if you write to us, we use your email address and message
                            only to reply to you.</li>
                        <li><strong>Hosting:</strong> like any website, our hosting provider may process standard
                            technical logs (e.g., IP address, browser type) strictly to deliver and secure the site.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

